  <dimension1_explanation>The AI's thinking went in a fundamentally wrong direction: it tried to minimize the number of queries by using composite N values (96, 60, 25, 49) to maximize information per query, exploring whether 2 or 3 queries could suffice. It never considered the standard solution's simple iterative binary approach of determining X mod 2^1, 2^2, ..., 2^6 step by step using 6 queries. The AI spent ~2000 lines analyzing p-adic valuations of composite N and obstacles with hard-to-separate pairs, but never arrived at or considered the iterative mod-2^k strategy.</dimension1_explanation>
  <dimension2_turning_point_type>multi_step_mod_p</dimension2_turning_point_type>
